.TH GWAY-RFID 1 "2026-10-27" "gway-rfid" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gway-rfid \- standalone RFID command cards and label utilities
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gway-rfid command write
.BI --script-file " FILE " --signing-key " PEM " --issuer " NAME"
.RI ( --image " FILE " | --reader " mfrc522 )"
.RI [ --label " TEXT ] [ --timeout " SECONDS ] [ --overwrite ]
.PP
.B gway-rfid command inspect
.RI ( --image " FILE " | --reader " mfrc522 )"
.RI [ --trusted-issuers " DIRECTORY ] [ --show-script ]
.PP
.B gway-rfid command run
.RI ( --image " FILE " | --reader " mfrc522 )"
.BI --trusted-issuers " DIRECTORY"
.RI [ --max-timeout " SECONDS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shell cards store complete UTF-8 POSIX shell programs in signed canonical CBOR
on a MIFARE Classic 1K card. No UID-to-command lookup is required.
The GWY1 shell format uses flag 1 and provides 736 bytes for the entire envelope.
Writes verify blocks before committing the header. Inspect never executes.
.PP
Run explicitly verifies a trusted Ed25519 issuer and executes /bin/sh with
program text on stdin, a minimal environment, suppressed output and a bounded
timeout. Root execution is prohibited. Trusted programs retain the invoking
account's filesystem and network access; this is not a sandbox.
The observation service does not execute command cards.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --overwrite
Required to replace an existing image or write a physical card.
.TP
.BI --card-key-file " FILE"
Protected file containing six raw access-key bytes. Defaults to factory key A.
.TP
.BI --card-key-type " A|B"
Authentication key type; defaults to A.
.TP
.BI --trusted-issuers " DIRECTORY"
Ed25519 public keys named issuer.pem. Required for run; optional for inspect.
.TP
.B --show-script
Include full program text in inspection JSON. Default output hides it.
.SH LABEL COMMANDS
Existing label preview, label print, printer devices and printer test commands
remain available. Use the command-specific --help for printing options.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Explicit run preserves normal shell exit codes. Errors and timeouts return 1.
.SH FILES
No default trust store is assumed; supply one explicitly. Images are exactly
1024 bytes and new images have mode 0600.
